<title>USA: CME names 1997 board election candidates.</title>
<headline>CME names 1997 board election candidates.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange (CME) on Friday listed 24 candidates running for 12 slots on its 34-person board of directors during the CME's annual election on Jan 16, 1997.</p>
<p>The exchange's nominees were listed in a notice to members distributed on the trading floor.</p>
<p>The exchange said the 12 full members running for six spots representing the CME division are: Thomas Bentley, Terrence Duffy, Philip Glass, Robert Haworth, Phillip Karafotas, Don Nadick, Paul Nelson, Irwin Rosen, William Salatich, John Sandner, Louis Schwartz, and Joel Stender.</p>
